      13 = 2^2 3 + 1 (which divides no solution of phi(x) = 36) is a Pierpont cuban prime of the second kind.

e. X-a AND X-b ARE THE SAME IDENTITY
   (n+1)^3 - n^3 = 3 n (n+1) + 1.  For the consecutive 3-smooth pair (n, n+1) = (3, 4):
     4^3 - 3^3 = 2^6 - 3^3 = 37 = 3*3*4 + 1 = 2^2 3^2 + 1.
   so 'cycle denominator of cell (6,3)' and 'cuban prime' are one fact about the pair (3,4).
